 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Consistency is key in collaborative coding, and I want you to start internalizing these practices from day one.",
  "We always include a single digit in our method names.",
  "I'm here to support you and ensure that you have a smooth onboarding process.",
  "Oliver, as you continue to work on your Python coding assignments, I want to emphasize the importance of clear and concise commenting.",
  "Always add comments to your code to explain complex logic, algorithms, or any non-obvious implementation details.",
  "This helps other developers understand your code, and it's a crucial practice for collaboration and future maintenance.",
  "Comments are essential for code documentation and should provide insight into your reasoning and any specific challenges you overcame.",
  "Don't skimp on them, and ensure they're meaningful.",
  "Unless specifically asked for input or assistance, I'd like you to refrain from initiating excessive conversations or seeking attention from your colleagues.",
  "It's important that we respect each other's time and maintain a productive environment.",
  "Now, moving on to some coding standards, I'd like you to start adopting a consistent naming convention for your variable names.",
  "From now on, all variable names should start with 'w_'.",
  "This helps us maintain a clear and distinct style within our codebases.",
  "Another aspect I want to emphasize is the importance of timely deliveries.",
  "I expect you to manage your tasks efficiently and deliver your assignments on time.",
  "If you ever anticipate delays, bring it to my attention immediately so we can address it together.",
  "Always ensure your code is properly documented, with clear comments explaining complex sections or logic.",
  "This helps your colleagues understand your work and facilitates maintenance and future updates."
 ],
